@TaslimOseni I noticed while working on improving our test suite that the homepage announcement is still shown in other locales even though it has long since expired. See this screenshot,

<img width="240" src="/uploads/890707a41b37a9b34e7167af05a74afc/005_fragment_home.png"></img>

I'm guessing there is an issue with matching the date in different languages. To reproduce, set your device to another locale for which the announcement is translated and open a fresh install of Ceno. We should fix this as soon as possible, I'm thinking that we should be able to use the date that is included in the `guid` field of the [rss-announce.xml](https://censorship.no/es/rss-announce.xml). Hopefully the fix is simple and we can squeeze it into v2.2.0.

## Summary

The latest version 2.7.0 doesn't show articles anymore unless I wipe data and restore a backup. The loading bar is almost full at the end, but nothing happens anymore.

## Steps to reproduce

Wipe data, restore backup and wait... I don't know how long, probably until the article cache time has expired?

